# BitCapital Research Pool: structural report for March–May 2026

## Period overview

This document presents a revised version of the internal BitCapital Research Pool report for March–May 2026. It is framed as a research-oriented publication: the emphasis is placed not only on the result, but also on context, pool configuration, sources of fragility, and limits of interpretation.

The observed period was characterized by market uncertainty and a consolidation phase following the completion of a downward move. Under these conditions, the central task was not market prediction as such, but management of the pool structure through asset reallocation, liquidity maintenance, and control of risk concentration.

Throughout the period, a constant calculation base of 100,000 USDT was used. The increase in value obtained at the end of each month was fixed as a separate result for that period rather than treated as an automatically reinvested base for the following month.

## Context and calculation logic

The BitCapital Research Pool is treated as an internal liquidity environment designed for applied management of asset structure and observation of system behavior under changing conditions. In this report, the result is not evaluated as the linear return of an abstract portfolio, but as the outcome of a specific pool configuration measured against an unchanged calculation base.

This approach matters for two reasons. First, it separates the result of an individual month from the cumulative effect of reinvestment. Second, it makes the comparison of different periods more transparent, because each monthly observation is measured against the same base of 100,000 USDT.

